        "base_3x3": "Both 288x288 bases repeated 3x3 and inspected at 1x and 4x, with exact 4x crops across the four-tile wrap intersection. The former slab/dash/puddle landmarks and conspicuous slush streaks are gone. The low-contrast pavement mottling stays subordinate in the dense and sparse scenes; no hard seam, tile frame or objectionable stamped grid remains at game scale. Compared with approved grass/plains summer and winter 3x3 controls.",
        "dense_to_sparse": "City, slums and industry each composited on the matching seasonal street base, densely planted through thinning to isolated buildings. All six scenes inspected at 1x and 4x. Exact 4x scenes are also saved as three adjoining panes so their pixels can be inspected without shrinking the whole image.",
        "one_cell_random_8x2": "Six seeded random 8x2 composites: city 0..5, slums 0..7 and industry 0..5, summer and winter. Every 48x48 source appears at least once in its composite. Inspected at 1x and 4x. These are transparent individual buildings: intentional space around a building is not a terrain seam, and deliberate reuse in a test scene is not a duplicate source variant.",
        "individual_8x": "All 76 sprites inspected at 8x on matching street backgrounds, grouped by season, category and canvas size with index labels. Both complete bases inspected at 8x in four non-overlapping 144x144 source quadrants each. Every sprite additionally inspected in 1x and 4x contact sheets.",
        "dimensions_and_placement": "All 78 required files present with the exact Part 3 dimensions. Both bases fully opaque. All sprites have only alpha 0 or 255, stand two transparent rows above the bottom edge and are centred within half a source pixel. No clipped source silhouettes or misplaced floating bases found.",
        "pixel_quality": "No blur, alpha antialiasing, stray matte fringe, pale halo or objectionable outline contamination found at 8x. Revised flat wall planes use crisp pixel clusters; they are intentional simplification rather than blurred texture. Remaining weathering in the inherited sprites is retained under the prior-pass rule.",
        "lighting_palette_and_style": "Compared with reference/jazz_age-marker0..3.png, reference/jazz_age-house.png and the approved out markers. Cream trim, terracotta brick, slate roofs, muted olive accents and dark outlines belong to that family. Upper-left highlights and darker right faces are consistent enough to ship. No material palette or pixel-density clash found against the approved round-2 tiles, paddies, grass or plains.",
        "winter": "Every winter sprite has a visibly changed roof/ledge snow treatment and preserves its summer structure. Revised snow caps are connected and do not erase the doors, window openings or stair routes. The revised industry-7 retains bounded roof openings beneath a coherent snow plane. The winter street is exposed cold pavement beneath the snow-covered buildings; the brief does not require it to be a solid snow field.",
        "diversity": "No exact RGBA duplicates. Side-by-side visual checks find distinct footprints, rooflines, proportions and uses within each category; no rejected near-duplicate pair. Summer/winter partners intentionally retain the same architecture.",
        "references": "Viewed the named jazz_age reference markers and house, approved out jazz_age markers, approved round-2 city/slums/industry in summer and winter, all four seasonal paddies, and all grass/plains seasonal bases and detail variants. Saved comparison sheets under the same review prefix.",
